        "english": "God Krishna concludes the third chapter on Karma Yoga by delivering the definitive master key to overcoming inner turmoil and desire. Having established that the conscious Self (*Ātman*) is transcendental and far superior to the gross body, senses, mind, and intellect, the seeker must anchor their identity in this supreme spiritual reality (*Buddheḥ paraṃ buddhvā*). By elevating and steadying the turbulent mind through this enlightened spiritual intellect (*Saṃstabhya ātmānam ātmanā*), one gains the transcendental strength necessary to conquer *Kāma*—the otherwise elusive, formidable enemy (*Durāsadam*) that deludes human consciousness. Thus, Krishna urges Arjuna to rise as a spiritual warrior and master his duties with fearless self-realization.",
